Revision history for Verksted

{{$NEXT}}
  - status and wait on a run still waiting for the Desktop part say whether
    a Verksted Desktop part has polled this profile and how long ago
    (desktop_last_poll_s); nothing is restarted because of it.
  - The Desktop status chip shows the window's note: "Agent-Teil nicht
    aktiviert" on a 404 from the plugin API, "Hermes Desktop zu alt für
    Verksted" when the host lacks profileRoutes, requestProfile,
    retainProfile or openSession; such a window starts nothing.
  - make package builds dist/verksted-<version>.zip from the committed
    tree; make install copies the committed package into a Hermes home under
    .dev/ and drops a stale Desktop copy.
  - The bundled skill tells a never-polled Desktop part from a closed
    Desktop, and its description says when to load it.
  - verksted cancel stops a running turn through prompt.cancel and reports it
    only once Hermes confirms; a run Hermes never saw ends cancelled.
    verksted send runs a follow-up turn in the same child session.
  - A lost submit confirmation repeats the identical submit; a gateway lost
    mid-turn leaves the run unknown and nothing is retried. Rückfragen left
    unanswered and blocked approvals are reported with the result.
  - Every task asks for a result block; listed outputs are checked against
    the workspace root (not_found, outside_workspace including symlink
    escapes, bad_path), only references are stored, and the Desktop run view
    lists them. The store migrates in place to schema v2.
  - .verksted.yaml is resolved from the plugin settings workspaces,
    allowed_profiles and toolset_ceiling: the walk starts at the outermost
    registered workspace (without one, at every ancestor); missing values
    inherit, lists only narrow and widening is refused; the file may hold
    only version, profile and toolsets, credentials and models are refused
    by name. A run may use another allowed profile on the same connection,
    the store stays with the parent. Resolved state, file hashes and
    fingerprint are frozen at run and shown by status and the Desktop part.
  - Folders are checked on the executing backend: canonical real path,
    byte-exact names, one active run per folder on a case-folded key.
    Windows drive paths only (\\?\ is stored plain, UNC and device paths are
    refused); a WSL backend maps Windows paths with Hermes' helper, elsewhere
    they are refused; files must stay inside the folder.
  - verksted tool (run, status, wait, send, cancel) stores every run with all start ids before anything starts it; SQLite
    run and claim store with claim generations; plugin API for claims and
    start steps; Desktop part that starts the run as a regular Hermes
    session after the toolset check and reports its result; make dev-env,
    make test, make doctor.
  - bundled Hermes skill verksted:verksted (recognises a workspace, picks the
    next workflow step, writes a self-contained task, reaches the tool
    directly or via tool_search/tool_call, handles every run state;
    questions and approvals stay with the user in the child's own chat);
    demo workspace examples/verksted-demo/ with steps 10-research and
    20-write. The skill covers send and cancel, result outputs and the
    topmost workspace root.
